  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <a href="/blog" class="text-gray-500 hover:text-orange-500 text-sm mb-6 block">&larr; Back to Blog</a>

    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">July 22, 2026 &middot; VPS Provider Review &middot; 14 min read</div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">RamNode VPS Review 2026: Hourly Billing from $2/mo</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-400">Long-running boutique VPS brand, now under InMotion Hosting. Five datacenters, crypto + Alipay payment stack, hourly billing across four product lines.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-1 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-1: What RamNode Is and Why It Matters in 2026</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">RamNode is a long-running boutique VPS brand whose registered trademark is now held by <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">InMotion Hosting, Inc.</a>, the Los Angeles-based hosting company founded in 2001. The brand historically operated as a small independent provider with a loyal developer following; the InMotion integration provides financial backing that lowers the going-concern risk associated with smaller indie hosts like Zappiehost.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">What distinguishes RamNode from the bulk of the US-hosted VPS market in 2026 is the combination of <strong>hourly billing without annual lock-in</strong> and an unusual payment stack: PayPal, credit card, crypto (multiple coins), and Alipay. The Alipay support is rare among US-headquartered providers and is a practical differentiator for buyers paying from CNY wallets who want US/EU compute without going through a Chinese-only provider like Aliyun.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300">The product line splits into five distinct tracks: <strong>Lite</strong> (IPv6-only from $2/mo), <strong>Standard</strong> (SSD KVM from $4/mo), <strong>Premium</strong> (NVMe from $14/mo), <strong>Storage</strong> (HDD from $4/mo), and <strong>VDS</strong> (dedicated CPU cores from $50/mo). For developers who want to spin a small box up for a few hours to test a workflow, then shut it down without losing money on an unused month, this is a more flexible model than the annual-prepay floor that <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd</a> and BandwagonHost are optimized for.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-2 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-2: Verified Pricing &mdash; Lite $2/mo, Standard $5/mo, Premium NVMe $14/mo, VDS $50/mo</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">All prices below were live on <code class="bg-gray-800 px-2 py-1 rounded">ramnode.com/pricing/</code> on 2026-07-22.</p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-orange-400 mb-2">Lite VPS &mdash; IPv6-only (EWR / LAX / NLX; SEA coming soon)</h3>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-6 space-y-1">
        <li>&bull; 1 GB RAM, 1 vCPU, 15 GB NVMe, 500 GB transfer &mdash; <strong>$2/mo</strong></li>
        <li>&bull; 2 GB RAM, 1 vCPU, 20 GB NVMe, 500 GB transfer &mdash; <strong>$3/mo</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-orange-400 mb-2">Standard VPS &mdash; SSD, virtualized compute</h3>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-6 space-y-1">
        <li>&bull; 512 MB / 1 vCPU / 20 GB SSD / 1 TB &mdash; $4/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 1 GB / 1 vCPU / 40 GB SSD / 2 TB &mdash; $5/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 2 GB / 2 vCPU / 80 GB SSD / 4 TB &mdash; $10/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 4 GB / 4 vCPU / 120 GB SSD / 8 TB &mdash; $20/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 8 GB / 4 vCPU / 180 GB SSD / 12 TB &mdash; $40/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 16 GB / 8 vCPU / 260 GB SSD / 14 TB &mdash; $80/mo</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-orange-400 mb-2">Premium VPS &mdash; NVMe, faster CPUs</h3>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-6 space-y-1">
        <li>&bull; 2 GB / 2 vCPU / 80 GB NVMe / 6 TB &mdash; <strong>$14/mo</strong> (entry NVMe)</li>
        <li>&bull; 4 GB / 4 vCPU / 120 GB NVMe / 10 TB &mdash; $24/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 8 GB / 4 vCPU / 200 GB NVMe / 14 TB &mdash; $48/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 16 GB / 8 vCPU / 400 GB NVMe / 16 TB &mdash; $96/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 32 GB / 16 vCPU / 600 GB NVMe / 18 TB &mdash; $192/mo</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-orange-400 mb-2">VDS &mdash; dedicated CPU cores (8-64 GB)</h3>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-6 space-y-1">
        <li>&bull; 8 GB / 2 dedicated cores / 200 GB NVMe / 10 TB &mdash; <strong>$50/mo</strong></li>
        <li>&bull; 16 GB / 4 dedicated cores / 400 GB NVMe / 20 TB &mdash; $90/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 32 GB / 8 dedicated cores / 800 GB NVMe / 40 TB &mdash; $170/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; 64 GB / 16 dedicated cores / 1600 GB NVMe / 60 TB &mdash; $320/mo</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-300">All tiers bill hourly. Adding block storage (EWR / LAX / NLX only) costs $0.085/GB/mo with $0.85 per 10 GB minimum, attachable via API to running cloud servers.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-3 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-3: Datacenter Footprint &mdash; 5 Locations, US East/West + NL</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">RamNode operates five datacenters as of July 2026, confirmed on the About page and pricing region codes:</p>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>&bull; <strong>Atlanta, GA</strong> (US East, region code ATL)</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>New Jersey</strong> (US East, region code EWR)</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Seattle, WA</strong> (US West, region code SEA &mdash; marked "coming soon" in pricing)</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Los Angeles, CA</strong> (US West, region code LAX)</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>The Netherlands</strong> (EU, region code NLX)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-300">The footprint covers the practical US East-Coast / West-Coast / transatlantic-EU triangle. It does not cover APAC, and Seattle is listed as a future location in the pricing matrix. For APAC-heavy workloads, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LightNode&rsquo;s 40+ locations from $7.70/mo</a> covers regions RamNode does not yet reach, and <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Vultr&rsquo;s 32+ locations</a> remain the broader global alternative.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-4 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-4: Hardware Stack &mdash; KVM Virtualization + Dedicated-CPU VDS</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">RamNode uses KVM virtualization across the Standard, Premium, and Storage tiers. The VDS tier reserves dedicated physical CPU cores (not oversubscribed), which is the right pick for noisy-neighbor-sensitive workloads like build servers, transcoding pipelines, or sustained CPU-bound services.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Storage options split by tier:</p>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>&bull; <strong>Standard tier</strong> uses SSD (not NVMe) &mdash; acceptable for general workloads, but slower than NVMe under sustained random-IO</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Premium tier</strong> uses NVMe, the right pick for database workloads and high-IO applications</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Storage tier</strong> uses HDD with very large capacity (up to 4 TB) and matching large transfer caps (up to 150 TB/mo) &mdash; archival and backup use cases only</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-300">There are no GPU instances across the product line. Buyers needing GPU compute should look at <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RunPod or Vast.ai</a> instead.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-5 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-5: Payment Stack &mdash; Crypto + Alipay + PayPal + Card</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">The payment stack is the most distinctive operational detail for RamNode. Verified live methods on 2026-07-22:</p>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm space-y-2 mb-4">
        <li>&bull; <strong>PayPal</strong> &mdash; standard for US VPS providers</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Credit Card</strong> &mdash; standard</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Crypto</strong> &mdash; multiple coins supported (Bitcoin, Ethereum, others); unusual at this price tier</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong>Alipay</strong> &mdash; very rare among US-headquartered VPS providers; relevant for buyers paying from CNY wallets who want US/EU compute</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-300">Combined with the hourly billing model, this is the closest match in the US VPS market for a buyer profile that wants maximum payment flexibility and no long-term commitment. The trade-off is that headline monthly prices are higher than <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd&rsquo;s annual-special floor at $10.98/yr</a> &mdash; the flexibility premium is real.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-6 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-6: Side-by-Side &mdash; RamNode vs RackNerd vs Vultr vs LightNode</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">For a budget-tier buyer in 2026, the four relevant providers to compare against RamNode are:</p>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm space-y-3 mb-4">
        <li>&bull; <strong><a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd</a></strong> &mdash; annual-special floor at <strong>$10.98/yr</strong> across 8 datacenters, unmetered 1 Gbps, DDoS included. Cheapest headline option for buyers willing to prepay annually. Loses to RamNode on flexibility (annual lock-in, no hourly billing, no Alipay) and on payment variety.</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong><a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Vultr</a></strong> &mdash; 32+ datacenters globally, $2.50/mo entry on regular cloud compute, broader geographic coverage. More expensive than RamNode&rsquo;s $2/mo Lite entry but with stronger APAC and broader hourly billing infrastructure. Vultr does not accept Alipay.</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong><a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LightNode</a></strong> &mdash; 40+ locations from $7.70/mo with $15 free credit, KVM VPS, hourly billing. Stronger APAC/Middle East/SA coverage than RamNode; weaker on crypto + Alipay payment variety. Wins for global-region buyers; loses on payment-stack diversity.</li>
        <li>&bull; <strong><a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">CrownCloud</a></strong> &mdash; KVM from $5/mo plus Ryzen 9950X VDS at $15/mo. Smaller datacenter footprint (LA + Frankfurt) but cheaper VDS entry than RamNode&rsquo;s $50/mo floor. Loses on payment variety and datacenter breadth.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-300">For the niche RamNode actually targets &mdash; developers wanting hourly billing + crypto + Alipay + US East/West + NL coverage &mdash; none of the four competitors offer the same combination.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-7 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-7: Use Cases &mdash; Who Should Pick RamNode in 2026</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4"><strong>Pick RamNode if:</strong></p>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm space-y-2 mb-6">
        <li>&bull; You want hourly billing without annual lock-in (testing, short-lived workloads, dev environments)</li>
        <li>&bull; You pay from a CNY wallet via Alipay and need US/EU compute (the rare combination)</li>
        <li>&bull; You prefer crypto payment and want a US-headquartered operator with financial backing</li>
        <li>&bull; You need US East/West + NL coverage specifically (not APAC)</li>
        <li>&bull; You want the cheapest entry price in vpstier&rsquo;s US/EU mix ($2/mo Lite tier)</li>
        <li>&bull; You need dedicated CPU cores via VDS tier starting at $50/mo</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4"><strong>Skip RamNode if:</strong></p>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm space-y-2">
        <li>&bull; You want the absolute cheapest VPS &mdash; <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd&rsquo;s $10.98/yr annual floor</a> wins</li>
        <li>&bull; You need APAC presence &mdash; pick <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LightNode</a> or <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Vultr</a></li>
        <li>&bull; You want unmetered bandwidth on a budget tier &mdash; none of RamNode&rsquo;s tiers are unmetered</li>
        <li>&bull; You need GPU instances &mdash; not available on RamNode</li>
        <li>&bull; You require IPv4-only on the cheapest tier &mdash; Lite is IPv6-only</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-8 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-8: The Final Verdict</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">RamNode is a focused pick for a specific buyer profile: developers who want hourly billing flexibility, the unusual crypto + Alipay payment stack, and US East/West + NL coverage without the annual lock-in that <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd</a> or BandwagonHost require. The InMotion Hosting ownership provides financial backing that&rsquo;s harder to find at indie-tier pricing.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">For the broader &ldquo;cheapest VPS available&rdquo; question, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd&rsquo;s annual-special floor at $10.98/yr across 8 datacenters</a> still wins on price-per-month. For APAC-heavy workloads, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LightNode&rsquo;s 40+ locations from $7.70/mo</a> or Vultr&rsquo;s 32+ global DCs are the right pick. But for the niche RamNode actually targets &mdash; hourly billed, multi-payment, US/EU-focused &mdash; it&rsquo;s the only US-headquartered provider offering this combination in 2026.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-4">Final rating: 4.0/5. Best for the right buyer, not the universal default.</p>
    </div>

